# Minimal API and Necessity First

Before adding or refactoring code, ask what the call site actually needs (data or behavior), then write the implementation. Do not let "replace the old method signature" drive the design.

## Avoid

- Wrapping a single call site in a bool/helper layer (for example `matchesX()` that is only `resolveX() != null`)
- **Simple utility classes with one reference**: one or two static methods whose logic is string assembly or a trivial mapping, called from a single listener/service in the whole repository — do not create a separate `*Renderer` / `*Helper` class; write it at the call site or in the existing owner class
- Defining the same rule in two places (regex, mapping, parsing logic)
- Mechanically preserving the old API shape during a refactor (the old method returned a bool, so a new bool wrapper appears) instead of checking whether the data flow changed
- Adding indirection just so the code "reads like before"

## Prefer

- **One resolution entry**: expose `resolveX()` when an enum/object is needed; when only a check is needed, inline `resolveX() != null` or use `Optional`
- **Draw the data flow before writing the API**: maintain each rule in exactly one place
- **Smallest public surface**: do not export a wrapper that serves one caller

## Examples

```java
// ❌ needless wrapper
public static boolean matchesVerbalSubmit(String input) {
    return resolveVerbalSubmitNode(input) != null;
}

// ✅ the call site states the intent directly
TradeRecordIntentNode verbal = TradeRecordIntentPatterns.resolveVerbalSubmitNode(input);
if (verbal != null) { ... }
```

```java
// ❌ referenced by one listener, and the logic only joins text with newlines
public final class SysMessageWorkWxTextRenderer {
    public static String render(...) { /* append into a StringBuilder */ }
}

// ✅ a private method on the listener, or on the message owner class
private String buildWorkWxText(...) { ... }
```

Self-check before committing: if you delete the new method/class and the call site only grows by a few clearer lines, do not add the new class.
